     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Simmer developers,</div><div><br></div><div>What is the difference between the <b>get_queue_size()</b> and <b>get_queue_count()</b> functions? In the official documentation on Simmer website there is no specific explanation for each one. In my current model I need to know during the simulation run the queue size of a resource to make a decision on a previous trajectory. The function I should use to access the current queue size during simulation is <b>get_queue_count()</b>?</div><div><br></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(68,68,68)\"><span><span><span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\"><span><span><span><span>Kind regards,</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></font></div><div><span><span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"font-size:13pt\">Ícaro Agostino</span></span><b><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"font-size:14pt\"></span><span style=\"font-size:14pt\"></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"></span></b></span><span style=\"color:rgb(64,64,64);font-size:11pt\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"font-size:13pt\">, </span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span><span><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Eng. MSc.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:calibri,sans-serif\"><span s